    "answer": {
      "short": "A",
      "worked": "The left end points up and the right end points down, so the leading coefficient is negative. This eliminates B.\n\nThe $x$-intercepts are $-2,\\ \\tfrac32,\\ 4$, so the factors are $(x+2)$, $(2x-3)$, $(x-4)$. This eliminates D, which has $x$-intercepts $2,\\ -\\tfrac32,\\ 4$.\n\nAt $x=0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{A: }y&=-(2)(-3)(-4)=-24\\\\\\text{C: }y&=-2(2)(-3)(-4)=-48\\end{align*}$$\nThe $y$-intercept is $-24$, so the answer is A.",
